('COD', '180', 'DR Congo', 23.5, -3.5, 70, 85, 75, 80, 70, array['Cu','Co','Au','3T','Li','Zn']::text[], 'Largest copper producer in Africa and roughly 70% of world cobalt. Eastern provinces contested by M23/AFC; the mining belt in Lualaba and Haut-Katanga is far from the front but exposed to export policy swings and border congestion.', array['Cobalt export quota administration (ARECOMS) and quota allocation disputes','Kasumbalesa border throughput and Lobito rail ramp-up','Washington and Doha peace tracks with Rwanda / M23','Manono lithium licence dispute (AVZ v. Zijin)']::text[], '[["2026-12", "Cobalt quota allocations for 2027 expected"], ["2027", "Lobito Atlantic Railway targets higher copper volumes; Zambia link financing"], ["2028-12", "General election due"]]'::jsonb, array['metals']::text[], 'africa'),
('ZMB', '894', 'Zambia', 27.8, -13.5, 40, 20, 45, 55, 25, array['Cu','Co','Au','Ni']::text[], 'Second-largest African copper producer with a stated goal of 3 Mt/y by 2031. Policy has been investor-friendly since 2021; power supply and transport capacity are the binding constraints.', array['Post-election policy continuity after the August 2026 general election (verify outcome)','Hydropower deficit at Kariba and tariff for mines','Lobito rail extension to the Copperbelt','Mopani and Konkola restart trajectories']::text[], '[["2026-08-13", "General election held (desk to confirm result and transition)"], ["2027", "Zambia Lobito rail link financing decisions"]]'::jsonb, array['metals']::text[], 'africa'),
('ZWE', '716', 'Zimbabwe', 29.9, -19, 60, 35, 70, 50, 55, array['Li','PGM','Au','Cu']::text[], 'Africa''s largest lithium producer and the second-largest PGM producer. Government pushes in-country processing through export bans; currency and sanctions on individuals complicate payments.', array['Lithium concentrate export ban scheduled for January 2027','ZiG currency stability and forex retention rules','Succession politics within ZANU-PF']::text[], '[["2027-01", "Lithium concentrate export ban scheduled"], ["2028", "General election due"]]'::jsonb, array['metals']::text[], 'africa'),
('ZAF', '710', 'South Africa', 25, -29, 35, 45, 35, 65, 15, array['PGM','Fe','Mn','Au','Cu','Prod']::text[], 'Deepest mining jurisdiction on the continent and the main outlet for the Copperbelt by road. Rail and port underperformance at Transnet and US tariff exposure are the live issues; politics stable under the coalition government.', array['Transnet rail volumes and private-operator access','US tariffs and AGOA status','Mining charter and energy policy under the GNU']::text[], '[["2026-11", "Local government elections window opens (to be scheduled)"], ["2027", "Transnet concession awards on key export lines"]]'::jsonb, array['metals','energy']::text[], 'africa'),
('GIN', '324', 'Guinea', -11, 10.5, 65, 40, 70, 45, 30, array['Bx','Fe','Au']::text[], 'World''s largest bauxite exporter and, with Simandou, a new top-tier iron ore source. Military-led government has revoked licences and reshaped the bauxite sector; civilian legitimacy contested.', array['Simandou ramp-up and Trans-Guinean railway reliability','Further bauxite licence revocations and local refining demands','Political consolidation after the December 2025 election']::text[], '[["2026", "Legislative elections expected"], ["2027", "Simandou reaches full export capacity (target)"]]'::jsonb, array['metals']::text[], 'africa'),
('MLI', '466', 'Mali', -2, 17, 80, 85, 80, 65, 55, array['Au','Li']::text[], 'Fourth-largest African gold producer under a military government that rewrote the mining code in 2023 and took direct control of Loulo-Gounkoto in 2025. Jihadist fuel blockades reached Bamako in late 2025.', array['Barrick settlement implementation and state share of Loulo-Gounkoto (verify current status)','JNIM pressure on fuel and road corridors to Senegal and Côte d''Ivoire','Goulamina lithium exports and state participation']::text[], '[["2027", "Transition timeline; junta leader granted renewable five-year term in 2025"]]'::jsonb, array['metals']::text[], 'africa'),
('GHA', '288', 'Ghana', -1.2, 7.9, 25, 20, 40, 30, 15, array['Au','Mn','Bx','Li','Crude','Gas']::text[], 'Africa''s largest gold producer with a stable democracy. State gold-buying agency GoldBod now centralises small-scale gold purchases; crackdown on illegal mining continues.', array['GoldBod export rules and effect on refiners','Ewoyaa lithium project permitting','Manganese (Nsuta) export policy']::text[], '[["2028-12", "General election due"]]'::jsonb, array['metals','energy']::text[], 'africa'),
('TZA', '834', 'Tanzania', 35, -6.5, 50, 30, 50, 40, 20, array['Au','Ni','Gr','U','Crude','Gas']::text[], 'Gateway port for the Copperbelt via Dar es Salaam and TAZARA, and a gold producer. Post-election violence in late 2025 showed political risk is higher than its reputation suggests.', array['Dar es Salaam port throughput under DP World concession','TAZARA revamp timeline (Chinese financing)','Kabanga nickel development']::text[], '[["2027", "TAZARA upgrade milestones"]]'::jsonb, array['metals','energy']::text[], 'africa'),
('MOZ', '508', 'Mozambique', 37, -17.5, 55, 60, 45, 55, 20, array['Gr','Au','Fe','LNG']::text[], 'Beira, Maputo and Nacala corridors serve Zimbabwe, Zambia and Malawi. Post-election unrest shut the Maputo corridor repeatedly in 2024-25; insurgency persists in Cabo Delgado near Balama graphite.', array['Cabo Delgado security and Balama operations','Beira corridor rail and port capacity','Opposition mobilisation around budget and fuel prices']::text[], '[["2029", "General election due"]]'::jsonb, array['metals','energy']::text[], 'africa'),
('AGO', '024', 'Angola', 17.5, -12.5, 40, 30, 40, 45, 25, array['Cu','Fe','Mn','Crude','LNG']::text[], 'Host of the Lobito Corridor, the shortest route from the Copperbelt to the Atlantic. Fuel-subsidy protests in 2025 were deadly; the port and railway are the strategic assets to watch.', array['Lobito Atlantic Railway volumes and Zambia extension','Fuel-price protests and urban unrest','2027 election positioning']::text[], '[["2027-08", "General election due"]]'::jsonb, array['metals','energy']::text[], 'africa'),
